## 15. SECURITY

### 15.1 Headers (via `next.config.js` or middleware)

| Header | Value |
|--------|-------|
| `X-Frame-Options` | `DENY` |
| `X-Content-Type-Options` | `nosniff` |
| `Referrer-Policy` | `strict-origin-when-cross-origin` |
| `Permissions-Policy` | `camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()` |
| Content-Security-Policy | Defined per environment |

### 15.2 Input security

- All user input sanitized server-side before database write
- SQL injection prevented by Prisma parameterized queries (never raw SQL without `.queryRaw` with parameters)
- XSS prevented by React's default escaping + no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization

### 15.3 CORS

- API routes: same-origin only in production
- Development: localhost origins allowed

