## 17. ERROR HANDLING

### 17.1 Client-side

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/app/not-found.tsx` | Custom 404 page |
| `src/app/error.tsx` | Global error boundary |
| `src/app/loading.tsx` | Global loading state (optional) |

- Error boundary catches rendering errors and shows user-friendly message
- 404 page offers navigation back to homepage and services
- No raw error messages shown to users

### 17.2 Server-side (API)

- All API route handlers wrapped in try/catch
- Errors logged server-side with context (route, timestamp, input shape)
- No stack traces returned to client in production
- Zod validation errors mapped to human-readable messages

### 17.3 External service failures

- S3 unavailable → upload form shows "service temporarily unavailable" message
- Database unavailable → static fallback content displayed
- AI widget unavailable → static CTA form shown (see §19)

