## 23. CHANGE MANAGEMENT

### 23.1 Branching strategy

| Branch | Purpose | Protection |
|--------|---------|-----------|
| `main` | Production-ready code | Protected: no direct commits |
| `develop` | Integration branch | Protected: no direct commits |
| `feat/*` | Feature development | — |
| `fix/*` | Bug fixes | — |
| `docs/*` | Documentation changes | — |

### 23.2 Pull request rules

- Every change requires a PR
- PR title follows Conventional Commits format
- Structural changes require MASTER_SPEC update **in the same PR**
- Minimum 1 reviewer approval before merge
- CI must pass (lint, type-check, tests) before merge

### 23.3 Deployment

| Environment | Source | Trigger |
|-------------|--------|---------|
| Production | `main` | Manual deploy after PR merge |
| Staging | `develop` | Auto-deploy on merge |
| Preview | `feat/*` | Auto-deploy per PR (Vercel preview) |

### 23.4 Rollback

- Revert the merge commit on `main`
- Database rollback: `pnpm prisma migrate reset` only on staging; production requires manual migration revert

